{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1545693-are-the-virtual-adepts-currently-the-most-jaded-mages","id":1545693,"title":"Are the virtual adepts currently the most jaded mages?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-11T07:51:31-08:00","id":1545693,"title":"Are the virtual adepts currently the most jaded mages?","content":"Some time ago, I was talking with a friend about how many old mages from the traditions were bitter with sleeper society. That's when he told me that the virtual adepts were the most bitter, jaded, and cynical of them all. Surprised, I asked him why since society has adopted the internet and modern technology, or so it looked like. He explained to me that sleeper society has adopted the consumer and addictive aspect of that technology, not its true potential. In the early 2000s, the virtual adepts genuinely believed that humanity was on the verge of some mass ascension to a virtual realm, but that didn't happen. In fact, what sleepers did was turn the internet into a cesspool of pettiness, porn, and profanity. A once infinite network of knowledge and learning has been debased and ruined so much, that it would be better to burn it down. If that's the case, just imagine what the virtual realm must look like. Every day the virtual adepts have to jump inside a place that has transformed into a grotesque parody of their ideals. It's the best example of the shit factor (the tendency of sleepers to take everything that mages create and drag it through the mud) you could imagine. As such, it's easy for me to imagine how the virtual adepts have become the most disillusioned mages among the traditions, all while the mages from the older traditions roll their eyes and say &quot;We told you so&quot;. Do you think there's any truth to this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 11-11-2024, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T08:19:38-08:00","id":1545695,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t say jaded so much as disillusioned. Jaded means bored. The Virtual Adepts aren\u2019t bored with the Internet, they hate it. They would love to tear it down and replace it with something newer and better like the OpNet from Trinity Continuum: Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T09:41:41-08:00","id":1545700,"title":"","content":"It is a little restrictive to say that the Virtual Adepts linked their entire ethos, worth, and success conditions to the internet. Certainly the way they internet has gone doesn't mesh amazingly well with their anarchic and slightly transhumanist tendencies. But to say they are disillusioned implies that the Tradition is a stagnant lot, that the VAs still have the same members and same goals that they did.<br /> <br /> There's a temptation to give the VAs a case of Brady Bunch Syndrome. What I mean by that is the Brady Bunch was a typical sitcom of its time, but after decades of syndication most viewers only saw it as a family stuck in the past. The world grew, the viewers grew, the reruns didn't. This culminated in the 90's movie (if anyone saw it) which essentially lampooned that out of touch quality. But that quality was, to my knowledge, never part of the original show. Realistically every member of the family would have grown with the times the way we all do.<br /> <br /> It's the same situation with the VAs. More than any other Tradition they come off as a very 90's creation, likely because of the heavy doses of Gen X attitudes, classic cyberpunk novels, and movie ideas of computers, internet, and VR. But there's no reason to think that the &quot;bleeding edge&quot; faction inexplicably got stuck in a 90's rut and never left. No, they brought in new members, dropped edgy phrases like &quot;bleeding edge,&quot; and continued adapting like they always have.<br /> <br /> After all, if they hadn't, they'd be too entrenched in 90s cynicism to be disillusioned anyways.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T13:31:08-08:00","id":1545708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1545693-are-the-virtual-adepts-currently-the-most-jaded-mages?p=1545700#post1545700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a little restrictive to say that the Virtual Adepts linked their entire ethos, worth, and success conditions to the internet. Certainly the way they internet has gone doesn't mesh amazingly well with their anarchic and slightly transhumanist tendencies. But to say they are disillusioned implies that the Tradition is a stagnant lot, that the VAs still have the same members and same goals that they did.<br /> <br /> There's a temptation to give the VAs a case of Brady Bunch Syndrome. What I mean by that is the Brady Bunch was a typical sitcom of its time, but after decades of syndication most viewers only saw it as a family stuck in the past. The world grew, the viewers grew, the reruns didn't. This culminated in the 90's movie (if anyone saw it) which essentially lampooned that out of touch quality. But that quality was, to my knowledge, never part of the original show. Realistically every member of the family would have grown with the times the way we all do.<br /> <br /> It's the same situation with the VAs. More than any other Tradition they come off as a very 90's creation, likely because of the heavy doses of Gen X attitudes, classic cyberpunk novels, and movie ideas of computers, internet, and VR. But there's no reason to think that the &quot;bleeding edge&quot; faction inexplicably got stuck in a 90's rut and never left. No, they brought in new members, dropped edgy phrases like &quot;bleeding edge,&quot; and continued adapting like they always have.<br /> <br /> After all, if they hadn't, they'd be too entrenched in 90s cynicism to be disillusioned anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>You raise a really good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T15:51:38-08:00","id":1545714,"title":"","content":"Revised actually did a lot of ground work for the VAs moving out of the 90s and into a more mundane digital future. <br /> <br /> That said... I'm not sure how you top the Euthanatos as the most jaded Tradition... they have mandated therapy sessions for their members so they don't go into Jhor Quiets from how jaded their philosophy makes them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}